We do a bluegreen deployment, if new version doesn't work, just stop using it and fade it out. Might tentatively put a new version of a service into operation, monitor them to make sure they're doing what they should do. Most of the instances are in service of the old version. When we're convinced that the new version is good we can up the number of instances of the new version. Gradually decrease the number of instances of the old version.

